  "visualBrief": "Historic Miami Mediterranean tower and attached plain west printing wing. Warm yellow stucco/pale cast-stone corner quoins and deep divided windows; nine plain three-column shaft levels. East portal has semicircular oak doors/fanlight, paired columns/capitals, broken scrolled pediment/original cartouche/abstract seated figures, iron balcony, glazed quatrefoils and large swept cornice/topwindow. Pierced base balconies/parapets/obelisks, raised front terrace/six entrance risers; rear plain divided casements/stepped central gable. Bracketed crown cornices, four real open roofed corner turrets, ornate square stage with arched/rectangular lights/roundels/cartouches, pierced balustrades/obelisks. Octagonal upper lantern with real cardinal arches/alternating blind niches and oculi, engaged columns/capitals, upper balcony/small windowed drum, paneled green copper dome/open beacon and original tall globe/cardinal-cross/ship vane. No neighboring campus/plaza/statue/interiors/scaffolds/photo textures.",
